# owl-has-key: a small runnable case for EYE RPO rules.
# Source: https://eyereasoner.github.io/eye/reasoning/rpo/owl-hasKey.n3
# Rules: MIT, Jos De Roo; sample data added for this example.
# The all-key-properties test uses log:forAllIn instead of list:setEqualTo.

@prefix : <http://example.org/>.
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix list: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/list#>.
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.

# Sample data
:Person owl:hasKey (:givenName :birthDate). :alice a :Person; :givenName "Alice"; :birthDate "1990-01-02". :alias a :Person; :givenName "Alice"; :birthDate "1990-01-02". :other a :Person; :givenName "Alice"; :birthDate "1991-03-04".

# Inference rules
{?C owl:hasKey ?L. ?X a ?C. ?Y a ?C. ?X log:notEqualTo ?Y.
 ({?P list:in ?L} {?X ?P ?Z. ?Y ?P ?Z}) log:forAllIn ?SCOPE} => {?X owl:sameAs ?Y}.
